2:T44d,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Article","headline":"Internal Authority vs. Positional Power: The Radical Ownership Framework","description":"Learn the difference between positional power and internal authority in leadership, plus how to use the Radical Ownership Script and Standard Audit to transform organizational culture.","datePublished":"2026-11-16","dateModified":"2026-11-24","articleSection":"Leadership","keywords":"internal authority leadership, positional power vs moral authority, radical ownership framework, leadership standard audit, leadership multiplier effect, how to build leaders without burnout, organizational culture accountability","mainEntityOfPage":{"@type":"WebPage","@id":"https://vibehyr.com/blog/internal-authority-radical-ownership-leadership"},"author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Keisha Solomon","jobTitle":"Founder & Master Architect, Vibe Hyr"},"publisher":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Vibe Hyr","url":"https://vibehyr.com","logo":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://vibehyr.com/icons/icon-512.png"}},"image":"https://vibehyr.com/images/og-image.png"}3:T546,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the difference between positional power and internal authority?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Positional power relies on a title, hierarchy, or threat of consequence to force external compliance. Internal authority is the self-regulated certainty, integrity, and emotional steadiness of a leader whom people choose to follow voluntarily because their standards and actions are congruent."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the Standard Audit in leadership?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The Standard Audit is a diagnostic principle from Vibe Hyr Leadership Course 01: you do not get the culture you ask for or write on the wall; you get the culture you tolerate and embody. Conducting a Standard Audit means identifying every gap between stated values and tolerated behaviors, starting with the leader's own habits."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How does the 4-stage Apprenticeship Loop prevent leadership burnout?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Instead of abdicating tasks too fast or hoarding responsibility forever, the 4-stage Apprenticeship Loop develops autonomous leaders through four deliberate phases: (1) I Do, You Watch; (2) I Do, You Help; (3) You Do, I Help; and (4) You Do, I Applaud."}}]}8:["slug","internal-authority-radical-ownership-leadership","d"]
