ap between stated values and tolerated behaviors, starting with the leader's own habits."}]]}],["$","div","2",{"className":"bg-black-2 border border-white/10 p-6 hover:border-orange-DEFAULT/30 transition-colors","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"font-body font-semibold text-white text-base mb-2","children":"How does the 4-stage Apprenticeship Loop prevent leadership burnout?"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"font-body text-grey-DEFAULT text-sm leading-relaxed","children":"Instead of abdicating tasks too fast or hoarding responsibility forever, the 4-stage Apprenticeship Loop develops autonomous leaders through four deliberate phases: (1) I Do, You Watch; (2) I Do, You Help; (3) You Do, I Help; and (4) You Do, I Applaud."}]]}]]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-12 pt-6 border-t border-white/8 flex items-center gap-2 flex-wrap","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-mono text-[0.48rem] tracking-[0.2em] uppercase text-grey-dark mr-2","children":"Topics:"}],[["$","span","internal authority leadership",{"className":"font-mono text-[0.46rem] tracking-[0.14em] uppercase px-2.5 py-1 bg-black-2 border border-white/10 text-grey-DEFAULT","children":"internal authority leadership"}],["$","span","positional power vs moral authority",{"className":"font-mono text-[0.46rem] tracking-[0.14em] uppercase px-2.5 py-1 bg-black-2 border border-white/10 text-grey-DEFAULT","children":"positional power vs moral authority"}],["$","span","radical ownership framework",{"className":"font-mono text-[0.46rem] tracking-[0.14em] uppercase px-2.5 py-1 bg-black-2 border border-white/10 text-grey-DEFAULT","children":"radical ownership framework"}],["$","span","leadership standard audit",{"className":"font-mono text-[0.46rem] tracking-[0.14em] uppercase px-2.5 py-1 bg-black-2 border border-white/10 text-grey-DEFAULT","children":"leadership standard audit"}],["$","span","leadership multiplier effect",{"className":"font-mono text-[0.46rem] tracking-[0.14em] uppercase px-2.5 py-1 bg-black